"JH" <no@email> wrote in news:vjbskf8c2p5b5b@corp.supernews.com:




> There are a couple of things that a lot of people seem deathly afraid
> of.

People are generally afraid of anything that can kill you in one turn or a 
very short nmber of turns - "instadeaths" and "delayed instadeaths". Pretty 
much each one of these has several means of avoidance - you simply need to 
pick one that works for you.

> For example, a lot of people talk about ;'s drowning them, so
> afraid in fact that many suggest carrying a stack of rocks or similar
> to squash them.  This caused my first two ascended characters (and one
> who didn't quite make it) to blessed genocide ;.  However, I once had
> a wizard with a +2 magicbane walk through the water plane, and he had
> no trouble whatsoever with drowning.  In fact, I've never had a ; grab
> me.  This whole business worries me, because I feel like it should
> have happened by now. 

To grab you they have to hit you; if you have a low AC, this will be rare. 
But you still need to prepare for the possibility. The simplest method is 
to never allow a grabbing water creature to get an attack on you - genocide 
and missile weapons (rocks are cheap, plentiful and don't have too many 
other uses) are examples of ways of doing this.

Another option is to make sure you don't actually need to breathe air - how 
can you drown then?

For an ascension-ready character however, such paranoia is not always 
necessary - I tend to make sure I am slippery (greased or oilskin outer 
armour) then whack them to death, if my attack is buff enough. If I'm using 
a greased cloak, I back off, use teleport away or similar as soon as the 
grease goes. I make sure I'm only ever next to one though, as it could get 
embarassing otherwise.

> Green slimes are another case.  My first character fought them all
> from a distance (V with Mojo) but later characters fought them hand to
> hand and never had to unslime themselves.

Green slimes are fairly harmless IME. Magic cancellation from armour is 
effective for them so with MC2 or 3 the number of successful attacks will 
be low. I simply carry a source of fire around - typically a wand or two 
(doubles for one-turn engraving), but I've never yet had to use it for un-
sliming. Given I dispatch slimes in 1 or 2 moves by the time I meet them, 
their chances of getting an attack in at all are very low, let alone 
getting past MC.

> Ditto for *trice's, I've
> only ever been stoned by one once, when a soldier hit me with a
> corpse, but their stoning attack never succeeds, as in I never even
> start the stoning process.

Yes, footrices seem to stone characters carrying lizard corpses about 1 
time in 100 or something - it's never happened to me in a regular game, and 
once when I was doing wizmode testing I got bored waiting for the 'trice to 
manage to stone me. Carrying a lizard corpse and a spare in your bag is 
plenty of insurance for live footrices.

Dead footrices are another story - I take great pains to keep track of them  
as it seems every hit from a rubber chicken is a successful stoning attack. 
Soldiers (and most gloved/stoning resistant monsters) are several times 
faster than a cockatrice too, multiplying the danger even more. If I'm 
surrounded, the 'trices are an extremely low priority, unless I reckon I 
can get there first and fancy wielding the corpse.

> So I guess my question is, am I *extremely* lucky that none of the
> above have happened to me, or are the above situations rare?

Sounds like my experience - just remember, one of these things *will* 
happen to you one day, so carry the means to survive each one as soon as 
you can, and always thereafter.


